      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the original test. It creates a local `NullReader` instance just to access the static `INSTANCE` field through it (confusing), then expects `reset()` to throw `IOException` because no mark has been set. I'll improve readability by accessing `INSTANCE` directly and adding a clear test name/comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The key change was replacing the confusing `nullReader0.INSTANCE.reset()` pattern (creating a local instance just to access a static field through it) with a direct `NullReader.INSTANCE.reset()` call, while preserving identical runtime behavior."
